$. What are the positive singular values of the $5\\times2$ matrix $A^{\\top}$?","options":["$4$ and $1$, the same as for $A$","$\\tfrac{1}{4}$ and $1$, the reciprocals","$16$ and $1$, the squares","Unknown, as $AA^{\\top}$ and $A^{\\top}A$ differ in size"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2224f419c3594bff6d6c9014","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_singular_value_06c82293_016_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A real $3\\times2$ matrix $A$ has singular values $\\sigma_1=4$ and $\\sigma_2=1$. Which value cannot occur as $\\|A\\boldsymbol{x}\\|$ for a unit vector $\\boldsymbol{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^2$?","options":["$1$","$2.5$","$4$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b9e5a67d5e7d0e44dad537a4","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_singular_value_06c82293_017_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A real $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with $m\\ge n$ has singular values $\\sigma_1\\ge\\cdots\\ge\\sigma_n\\ge0$. What are the singular values of the symmetric $n\\times n$ matrix $A^{\\top}A$?","options":["$\\sigma_1,\\ldots,\\sigma_n$: multiplying by $A^{\\top}$ adds no stretching","$\\sigma_1^2,\\ldots,\\sigma_n^2$: the eigenvalues of the symmetric $A^{\\top}A$","$\\sqrt{\\sigma_1},\\ldots,\\sqrt{\\sigma_n}$: one more square root of each value","$\\sigma_1^4,\\ldots,\\sigma_n^4$: the eigenvalues of $(A^{\\top}A)^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"90db13b349c6bcadf1153a1a","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_singular_value_06c82293_019_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\0&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}$, a $3\\times2$ matrix with no eigenvalues. What are its singular values $\\sigma_1\\ge\\sigma_2$?","options":["$9$ and $1$","$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$","$3$ and $1$","$\\sqrt{10}$ and $0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9a28d7f517826e6341bc705e","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_singular_value_06c82293_020_curated20261027_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For which real $a$ does $A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\2&a\\end{pmatrix}$ have a zero singular value?","options":["Only $a=-4$","Only $a=2$","No $a$, since singular values are positive","Only $a=4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c54184394df5fc73a515c5c2","time_limit":30}]}}